1970-01-03\\\"\\r\\n3$\\\"c'\\\"$false$NaN$\\\"1970-01-04\\\"\\r\\n\";","+            let expect = \"\\\"1\\\"$\\\"a\\\"$\\\"true\\\"$\\\"1.1\\\"$\\\"1970-01-02\\\"\\r\\n\\\"2\\\"$\\\"b\\\"\\\"\\\"$\\\"true\\\"$\\\"2.2\\\"$\\\"1970-01-03\\\"\\r\\n\\\"3\\\"$\\\"c'\\\"$\\\"false\\\"$\\\"NaN\\\"$\\\"1970-01-04\\\"\\r\\n\";","             assert_eq!(&csv_block, expect);","         }","         Ok(())","     }"," ","+    #[test]","+    fn test_empty_binary_output() -> Result<()> {","+        let (schema, block) = gen_schema_and_block(","+            vec![TableField::new(","+                \"binary\",","+                TableDataType::Binary.wrap_nullable(),","+            )],","+            vec![BinaryType::from_opt_data(vec![","+                Some(b\"\".as_slice()),","+                None,","+                Some(b\"\\xff\".as_slice()),","+            ])],","+        );","+        let mut formatter = get_output_format_clickhouse(\"tsv\", schema)?;","+        assert_eq!(formatter.serialize_block(&block)?, b\"\\n\\\\N\\nFF\\n\");","+        Ok(())","+    }","+","     #[test]","     fn test_null() -> Result<()> {","         let (schema, block) = gen_schema_and_block(","@@ -281,7 +300,7 @@ mod test {","         let buffer = output_format.serialize_block(&block)?;"," ","         let csv_block = String::from_utf8(buffer)?;","-        let expect = \"1\\x01\\\"a\\\"\\x01true\\x011.1\\x01\\\"1970-01-02\\\"\\r\\n2\\x01\\\"b\\\"\\\"\\\"\\x01true\\x012.2\\x01\\\"1970-01-03\\\"\\r\\n3\\x01\\\"c'\\\"\\x01false\\x01NaN\\x01\\\"1970-01-04\\\"\\r\\n\";","+        let expect = \"\\\"1\\\"\\x01\\\"a\\\"\\x01\\\"true\\\"\\x01\\\"1.1\\\"\\x01\\\"1970-01-02\\\"\\r\\n\\\"2\\\"\\x01\\\"b\\\"\\\"\\\"\\x01\\\"true\\\"\\x01\\\"2.2\\\"\\x01\\\"1970-01-03\\\"\\r\\n\\\"3\\\"\\x01\\\"c'\\\"\\x01\\\"false\\\"\\x01\\\"NaN\\\"\\x01\\\"1970-01-04\\\"\\r\\n\";","         assert_eq!(&csv_block, expect);"," ","         Ok(())"],"additions":21,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/query/storages/common/cache/tests/it/kinds/stability.rs","lines":["@@ -31,8 +31,9 @@ const THREADS: u64 = 8;"," const OPS: usize = 2_000;"," "," /// Threads mixing every kind on a small cache, while capacities change and memory pressure","-/// reclaims. Once nobody holds a value, every byte charged is a byte cached, within capacity;","-/// once every kind is turned off, nothing stays charged.","+/// reclaims. Once nobody holds a value, every byte charged is a byte cached. Reapplying shared","+/// limits reclaims entries that were pinned during a resize; turning every kind off clears","+/// all charges."," #[test]"," fn test_every_kind_under_concurrency() {","     for backend in Backend::ALL {","@@ -48,6 +49,21 @@ fn test_every_kind_under_concurrency() {","             thread.join().unwrap();","         }"," ","+        if backend == Backend::Shared {","+            // A resize cannot reclaim pinned entries. Dropping the workers' handles does not","+            // evict them from the cache, so reapply each limit now that all entries are unheld.","+            for row in manager","+                .rows()","+                .iter()","+                .filter(|r| r.kind.is_some() && r.pool.is_some())","+            {","+                assert_eq!(row.size, row.in_cache_size, \"{backend:?} {}\", row.name);","+                if let Some(capacity) = row.capacity {","+                    manager.set_cache_capacity(&row.name, capacity).unwrap();","+                }","+            }","+        }","+","         for row in manager","             .rows()","             .iter()","@@ -55,13 +71,15 @@ fn test_every_kind_under_concurrency() {","         {","             assert_eq!(row.size, row.in_cache_size, \"{backend:?} {}\", row.name);","             match (row.capacity, row.unit) {","-                (Some(cap), Unit::Bytes) => assert!(row.in_cache_size <= cap, \"{}\", row.name),","-                (Some(cap), Unit::Count) => assert!(row.num_items <= cap, \"{}\", row.name),","+                (Some(cap), Unit::Bytes) => {","+                    assert!(row.in_cache_size <= cap, \"{backend:?} {row:?}\")","+                }","+                (Some(cap), Unit::Count) => assert!(row.num_items <= cap, \"{backend:?} {row:?}\"),","                 (None, _) => {}","             }","         }","         for pool in manager.rows().iter().filter(|r| r.kind.is_none()) {","-            assert!(pool.size <= pool.capacity.unwrap(), \"{}\", pool.name);","+            assert!(pool.size <= pool.capacity.unwrap(), \"{backend:?} {pool:?}\");","         }"," ","         for kind in CacheKind::all() {"],"additions":23,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/query/storages/common/cache/tests/it/shared/kind_limit.rs","lines":["@@ -256,3 +256,27 @@ fn test_concurrent_turnover_stays_within_the_limit() {","     assert_eq!(events.rejected_kind_limit, 0);","     assert_eq!(events.evicted_for_capacity, (THREADS * 500 - 50) as u64);"," }","+","+/// Releasing a pinned handle does not itself evict the cached value. Reapplying the limit","+/// after readers finish must reclaim what the earlier resize could not.","+#[test]","+fn test_reapplying_limit_reclaims_previously_held_entries() {","+    let store = one_shard_store(10_000);","+    let cache = cache(&store, meta_kind());","+    let live = Live::default();","+    let held = cache.put(\"held\", live.item(100));","+","+    store.set_kind_limit(meta_kind(), KindLimit::bytes(50));","+    let kind = store.kind_stats(meta_kind());","+    assert_eq!((kind.resident, kind.in_cache, kind.items), (100, 100, 1));","+    assert!(!cache.put(\"new\", live.item(10)).is_charged());","+","+    drop(held);","+    let kind = store.kind_stats(meta_kind());","+    assert_eq!((kind.resident, kind.in_cache, kind.items), (100, 100, 1));","+    store.set_kind_limit(meta_kind(), KindLimit::bytes(50));","+    let kind = store.kind_stats(meta_kind());","+    assert_eq!((kind.resident, kind.in_cache, kind.items), (0, 0, 0));","+    assert_eq!(live.co